<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  macOS code-signing entitlements for Ship Studio.

  DO NOT STRIP com.apple.security.automation.apple-events.

  Release builds are notarized and therefore run under the hardened runtime,
  which blocks Apple Events outright unless this entitlement is present. Ship
  Studio needs it for exactly one feature: the opt-in Spotify widget
  (src-tauri/src/commands/spotify.rs), which reads "now playing" state and
  drives play/pause/next/seek/volume via osascript against Spotify.app.

  Without it the widget fails with -1743 in every shipped build and there is no
  user-facing fix — the macOS Automation prompt never even appears, because the
  process is not entitled to ask. Dev builds are ad-hoc signed and work without
  it, so removing this will look harmless locally and only break in release.

  The entitlement grants the ability to *ask*; the user still approves Spotify
  automation in System Settings → Privacy & Security → Automation on first use.

  Deliberately minimal: no App Sandbox keys, no other Apple Events scoping, and
  nothing that affects the Windows or Linux bundles.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
